\title{Find a byte in a \code{\verb~|String~} with scalable vectors}
\taxon{Example}
\date{2026-11-13}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{simd}
\tag{example}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The \code{\verb~|memchr~} loop of SVE and RVV: one loop, no scalar remainder. The string is pinned while only its data pointer is in use.}
\pre{\verb~|
import core::ptr;
import core::simd;
import core::ptr::PtrArithFlag;
import std::string::String;

// The index of the first `needle` in `s`, or the length of `s`.
pub fn find(s: String, needle: u8) -> u64 {
    let len = s.len();
    core::object::unsafe_inc(s);
    let base = s.unsafe_data_ptr();
    let width = simd::lanes<Simd<[u8; [16]]>>();
    let wanted = simd::splat<Simd<[u8; [16]]>>(needle);
    let zero = simd::splat<Simd<[u8; [16]]>>(0);
    let (at, hit) = while [i = 0, hit = len] (i < len && hit == len) {
        let live = simd::mask_first<Simd<[bool; [16]]>>(len - i);
        let chunk = simd::load<Simd<[u8; [16]]>>(
            ptr::offset(base, i as i64, PtrArithFlag::Inbounds), live, zero);
        let found = simd::eq(chunk, wanted, live);
        let here = if simd::any(found) { i + simd::first_set(found) } else { len };
        (i + width, here)
    };
    core::object::unsafe_dec(s);
    hit
}
~}
\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|mask_first(len - i)~} covers the whole vector until the last iteration and only the remaining bytes there, so nothing is read past the end.}
\li{The comparison takes the mask too, so the padding lanes of the last chunk cannot match.}
\li{\code{\verb~|unsafe_inc~} and \code{\verb~|unsafe_dec~} bracket the region where the buffer is reachable only through \code{\verb~|base~}. Without them the string may be released after \code{\verb~|s.unsafe_data_ptr()~}, its last ordinary use.}
}
\p{Belongs to [SIMD vectors](design-simd-vectors). Written against the draft; not compiled.}
